# setuptools-scm puts every git-tracked file in the sdist, which is the right default for source
# but wrong for `assets/`: the demo GIF and the two architecture figures are README illustrations
# that GitHub renders and nothing in the package reads. They were 1.4 MB of a 2.3 MB sdist, so
# every install paid to download them.
#
# The shipped README.md still points at them relatively. That link resolves on GitHub and nowhere
# else, which is already true of every relative target in it — the reason `project.readme` is
# README.pypi.md, whose links are all absolute (tests/test_packaging.py pins both halves).
prune assets
